IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTION 7: EXCEPTIONS.
--
-- What is encoded: s 7(1) to (5), the contracts in which section 2 confers no right on a third party (and the
-- carve-back of s 7(5)), and s 7(6) and (7), the definitions the carriage exception uses.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Each exception is a flat negative
-- ("does not confer any right") with its own scope.  Its function is "section 2 confers a right on the third party in
-- the case of the contract": JUST FALSE inside the scope (the text says no), NOTHING outside it (the text does not
-- say that section 2 does confer a right there; that is section 2's business).
--
-- BORROWED TERMS.  "negotiable instrument", a contract binding under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967, an
-- LLP registration document, "contract of employment", and the meanings the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives are other
-- laws' terms, and are asked as facts.  Where the Minister has to prescribe by order (the written law for a rail or
-- road Convention) the fact is asked, never assumed.

§ `Section 7(1) to (4) -- contracts in which section 2 confers no right`

-- src:260 | 7.—(1) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the
-- src:261 | case of a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other
-- src:262 | negotiable instrument.
@ref s 7(1) (src:260-262)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only "a contract on a bill of exchange, promissory note or other negotiable instrument"; another contract is outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:264 | (2) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of
-- src:265 | any contract binding on a company and its members under section 39
-- src:266 | of the Companies Act 1967.
@ref s 7(2) (src:264-266)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of any contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only "any contract binding on a company and its members under section 39 of the Companies Act 1967"; another contract is outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:268 | (3) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of
-- src:269 | any registration document of a limited liability partnership registered
-- src:270 | under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 or any limited
-- src:271 | liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act.
@ref s 7(3) (src:268-271)
GIVEN `the contract is a registration document of a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract is a limited liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a registration document of a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
       OR `the contract is a limited liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of any registration document of a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005 or any limited liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only a registration document of a limited liability partnership or a limited liability partnership agreement as defined in that Act; another contract is outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:275 | (4) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party to enforce
-- src:276 | any term of a contract of employment against an employee.
@ref s 7(4) (src:275-276)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party seeks to enforce the term against an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) section 2 confers a right on the third party to enforce a term of the contract of employment against an employee` MEANS
    IF `the contract is a contract of employment` AND `the third party seeks to enforce the term against an employee`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party to enforce any term of a contract of employment against an employee."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only enforcement "of a contract of employment against an employee"; another contract, or enforcement against someone else, is outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 7(6) and (7) -- the definitions the carriage exception uses`

-- "bill of lading", "sea waybill" and "ship's delivery order" have the meanings given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992,
-- which is not among the sources: the meaning is the borrowed fact the person states.
-- src:324 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6), “bill of lading”, “sea
-- src:325 | waybill” and “ship’s delivery order” have the meanings given by the
-- src:326 | Bills of Lading Act 1992.
@ref s 7(7) (src:324-326)
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Shipping document`
      `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(7) the document has the meaning given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992 for its name` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is "given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992", which is not among the sources, so the person's statement of it is the answer, and NOTHING when not stated
    WHEN `a bill of lading` THEN `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is "given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992", which is not among the sources, so the person's statement of it is the answer, and NOTHING when not stated
    WHEN `a sea waybill` THEN `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is "given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992", which is not among the sources, so the person's statement of it is the answer, and NOTHING when not stated
    WHEN `a ship's delivery order` THEN `the Bills of Lading Act 1992 gives the document that name`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 7(7) speaks only of "bill of lading", "sea waybill" and "ship's delivery order"
    WHEN `any other document` THEN NOTHING

-- src:312 | “contract for the carriage of goods by sea” means a contract of
-- src:313 | carriage —
-- src:315 | (a) contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea
-- src:316 | waybill; or
-- src:318 | (b) under or for the purposes of which there is given an
-- src:319 | undertaking which is contained in a ship’s delivery
-- src:320 | order.
@ref s 7(6) "contract for the carriage of goods by sea" (src:312-320)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract of carriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(6) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“contract for the carriage of goods by sea” means a contract of carriage — (a) contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill; or (b) under or for the purposes of which there is given an undertaking which is contained in a ship’s delivery order."
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a document is a bill of lading, sea waybill or ship's delivery order has the meaning given by the Bills of Lading Act 1992 (s 7(7)), so the limbs are the person's statements
    `three-valued AND`
        (`a stated fact` `the contract is a contract of carriage`)
        (`three-valued OR` `it is contained in or evidenced by a bill of lading or sea waybill` `an undertaking contained in a ship's delivery order is given under or for the purposes of it`)

-- src:292 | “appropriate international transport convention” means —
-- src:294 | (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by
-- src:295 | air, the Convention which has the force of law in
-- src:296 | Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air
-- src:297 | Act 1988;
-- src:299 | (b) in relation to a contract for the carriage of goods by
-- src:300 | rail, such Convention which has the force of law in
-- src:301 | Singapore under such written law as the Minister
-- src:302 | may by order prescribe; and
-- src:307 | (c) in relation to a contract for the carriage of goods by
-- src:308 | road, such Convention which has the force of law in
-- src:309 | Singapore under such written law as the Minister
-- src:310 | may by order prescribe;
@ref s 7(6) "appropriate international transport convention" (src:292-310)
GIVEN `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage`
      `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under a written law the Minister has by order prescribed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(6) the Convention is the appropriate international transport convention for the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the mode of carriage`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the air limb is "the Convention which has the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988", a fact about another Act, stated by the person
    WHEN `carriage of cargo by air` THEN `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under section 3 of the Carriage by Air Act 1988`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rail limb is a Convention with the force of law "under such written law as the Minister may by order prescribe"; the order is not among the sources, so the person's statement of it is the answer
    WHEN `carriage of goods by rail` THEN `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under a written law the Minister has by order prescribed`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the road limb is a Convention with the force of law "under such written law as the Minister may by order prescribe"; the order is not among the sources, so the person's statement of it is the answer
    WHEN `carriage of goods by road` THEN `the Convention has the force of law in Singapore under a written law the Minister has by order prescribed`
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“appropriate international transport convention” means — (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by air ...; (b) ... the carriage of goods by rail ...; and (c) ... the carriage of goods by road ..." has no limb for a carriage by sea
    WHEN `carriage by sea` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“appropriate international transport convention” means — (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by air ...; (b) ... the carriage of goods by rail ...; and (c) ... the carriage of goods by road ..." has no limb for a carriage by air of something other than cargo (passengers, say): limb (a) is for "cargo by air" only
    WHEN `carriage by air of something other than cargo, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“appropriate international transport convention” means — (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by air ...; (b) ... the carriage of goods by rail ...; and (c) ... the carriage of goods by road ..." has no limb for a carriage by rail of something other than goods (passengers, say): limb (b) is for "goods by rail" only
    WHEN `carriage by rail of something other than goods, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“appropriate international transport convention” means — (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by air ...; (b) ... the carriage of goods by rail ...; and (c) ... the carriage of goods by road ..." has no limb for a carriage by road of something other than goods (passengers, say): limb (c) is for "goods by road" only
    WHEN `carriage by road of something other than goods, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a definition that says "means"): "“appropriate international transport convention” means — (a) in relation to a contract for the carriage of cargo by air ...; (b) ... the carriage of goods by rail ...; and (c) ... the carriage of goods by road ..." has no limb for a carriage by another mode
    WHEN `carriage by some other mode` THEN JUST FALSE

§ `Section 7(5) -- carriage contracts`

-- src:278 | (5) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case
-- src:279 | of —
-- src:281 | (a) a contract for the carriage of goods by sea; or
@ref s 7(5)(a) (src:278-281)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea as s 7(6) defines it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5)(a) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` MEANS
    `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea as s 7(6) defines it`

-- src:278 | (5) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case
-- src:279 | of —
-- src:283 | (b) a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for
-- src:284 | the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of
-- src:285 | the appropriate international transport convention,
@ref s 7(5)(b) (src:278-285)
GIVEN `the mode of carriage` IS A `Mode of carriage`
      `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5)(b) the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the mode of carriage`
    WHEN `carriage of cargo by air` THEN `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`
    WHEN `carriage of goods by rail` THEN `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`
    WHEN `carriage of goods by road` THEN `the contract is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`
    -- FALSE-kind (a closed description): "a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air" does not describe a carriage by sea
    WHEN `carriage by sea` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a closed description): "a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air" does not describe a carriage by air of something other than cargo (passengers, say): the word is "cargo"
    WHEN `carriage by air of something other than cargo, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a closed description): "a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air" does not describe a carriage by rail of something other than goods (passengers, say): the word is "goods"
    WHEN `carriage by rail of something other than goods, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a closed description): "a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air" does not describe a carriage by road of something other than goods (passengers, say): the word is "goods"
    WHEN `carriage by road of something other than goods, such as passengers` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (a closed description): "a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air" does not describe a carriage by another mode
    WHEN `carriage by some other mode` THEN JUST FALSE

-- Judgment call QA: the exception "except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third party of
-- an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract" lifts the bar for that case.  Here a lifted bar grants
-- nothing (NOTHING); the grant is the next function, whose words are the text's own "may ... avail".
-- src:278 | (5) Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case
-- src:279 | of —
-- src:281 | (a) a contract for the carriage of goods by sea; or
-- src:283 | (b) a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for
-- src:284 | the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of
-- src:285 | the appropriate international transport convention,
-- src:287 | except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third
-- src:288 | party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract.
@ref s 7(5) (src:278-288)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party seeks only to avail itself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5) section 2 confers a right on the third party in the case of the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `three-valued OR` `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the third party seeks only to avail itself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording; judgment call QA): "except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract" lifts the bar, and a lifted bar grants nothing
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not confer any right on a third party in the case of — (a) a contract for the carriage of goods by sea; or (b) a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention"
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only the contracts of (a) and (b); another contract is outside it
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the contract is one of (a) or (b) has not been stated
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:287 | except that a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third
-- src:288 | party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract.
@ref s 7(5) the exception (src:287-288)
GIVEN `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party seeks only to avail itself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5) the third party may in reliance on section 2 avail of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract` MEANS
    IF `the third party seeks only to avail itself of an exclusion or limitation of liability in the contract`
    THEN CONSIDER `three-valued OR` `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by sea` `the contract is a contract for the carriage of goods by rail or road, or for the carriage of cargo by air, which is subject to the rules of the appropriate international transport convention`
         -- TRUE: the text's own "a third party may in reliance on that section avail the third party of an exclusion or limitation of liability in such a contract"; the right itself is still section 2's
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in such a contract" means a contract of (a) or (b); another contract is outside it
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the contract is one of (a) or (b) has not been stated
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only a third party who avails itself "of an exclusion or limitation of liability"; a claim for anything else stays under the bar above
    ELSE NOTHING
